{"key":"enterprise/T1070.009","id":"T1070.009","name":"Clear Persistence","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1070","tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may clear artifacts associated with previously established persistence on a host system to remove evidence of their activity. This may involve various actions, such as removing services, deleting executables, Modify Registry, Plist File Modification, or other methods of cleanup to prevent defenders from collecting evidence of their persistent presence. Adversaries may also delete accounts previously created to maintain persistence…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1070/009","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--d2c4e5ea-dbdf-4113-805a-b1e2a337fb33","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.717Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0040","name":"File Deletion","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0040","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--e905dad2-00d6-477c-97e8-800427abd0e8","page":"telemetry/DC0040/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0001","name":"Scheduled Job Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0001","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--f42df6f0-6395-4f0c-9376-525a031f00c3","page":"telemetry/DC0001/"},{"id":"DC0009","name":"User Account Deletion","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0009","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--d6257b8e-869c-41c0-87